# The whole reason /lander needed catching: a parking page cached for a year.
# HTML revalidates from now on, so a bad deploy or another domain move cannot
# strand somebody on a copy that no longer exists. Assets keep a real TTL --
# they are versioned by content and never change under the same name.
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

/*.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
